What is a process?
	A process is an instance of a program in execution. It contains the program code along with its current state, memory, CPU registers, program counter, and allocated system resources. The operating system manages processes to enable multitasking and resource sharing.
	
What is PCB (Process Control Block)?
	The OS stores process information in a PCB.

	It contains:

		Process ID (PID)
		Process state
		Program Counter
		CPU registers
		Scheduling information
		Memory information
		Open files

	Without PCB, the OS would have no idea what the process was doing before it got interrupted.

