Can multiple processes share the same code?

	Yes. Multiple processes can share the same read-only code segment while maintaining separate memory spaces for data, stack, and heap.
	
A process is an instance of a program that is currently executing. It includes the program code, its execution state, memory segments such as stack and heap, CPU registers, and other resources allocated by the operating system. The OS tracks and manages processes using a Process Control Block (PCB), allowing multiple processes to execute concurrently through scheduling.

